  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a downtrend or consolidation near support (e.g., 83-89 range), the model systematically overestimates by 5-10% because it ignores immediate mean reversion to historical averages.",
    "The model exhibits severe lag in reacting to sudden sentiment spikes; when sentiment jumps from 0.00 to 0.20+, actual prices often drop further before recovering, causing the model to overshoot upward targets by 5-15%.",
    "In volatile regimes (e.g., May 2023), the model fails to capture high-frequency volatility and trend reversals, resulting in a consistent bias toward smooth, linear growth that contradicts true outcome jaggedness.",
    "When sentiment history is flat or low (0.00-0.20) despite rising prices, the model assumes continuation but actual outcomes frequently reverse sharply within 5-10 days.",
    "The model's 30-day horizon consistently underestimates the magnitude of mean reversion events, predicting gradual corrections instead of sharp V-shapes or deep drops."
  ]
